IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `oapa-nouns`

-- Offences against the Person Act 1861 -- LAYER 1: ACTS CAUSING OR TENDING TO CAUSE
-- DANGER TO LIFE OR BODILY HARM, SECOND GROUP (sections 26 to 31): neglect of an
-- apprentice or servant, exposing a young child, explosions and explosives, and spring
-- guns and man traps.
--
-- "unlawfully", "maliciously", "wilfully", "knowingly": none is defined in the text;
-- each is a fact the person states.

§ `Acts causing or tending to cause Danger to Life or Bodily Harm: sections 26 to 31`

§§ `Section 26: not providing apprentices or servants with food, &c. whereby life is endangered`

-- src:40 | 26 Not providing apprentices or servants with food, &c. whereby life is endangered.
-- src:41 | Whosoever, being legally liable, either as a master or mistress, to provide for any apprentice or servant necessary food, clothing, or lodging, shall wilfully and without lawful excuse refuse or neglect to provide the same, or shall unlawfully and maliciously do or cause to be done any bodily harm to any such apprentice or servant, so that the life of such apprentice or servant shall be endangered, or the health of such apprentice or servant shall have been or shall be likely to be permanently injured, shall be guilty of a misdemeanor, and being convicted thereof shall be liable . . . to be kept in penal servitude . . .
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 26 (src:40-41)
-- Two ways in (either): (1) being legally liable as a master or mistress to provide an
-- apprentice or servant with necessary food, clothing or lodging, wilfully and without
-- lawful excuse refusing or neglecting to provide it; (2) unlawfully and maliciously
-- doing or causing to be done any bodily harm to such an apprentice or servant.  And a
-- result (either): "so that the life of such apprentice or servant shall be
-- endangered, or the health of such apprentice or servant shall have been or shall be
-- likely to be permanently injured".
-- FORK (see NOTES.md): the encoding reads the result clause as governing BOTH ways in.
-- The "legal liability" is a duty the Act does not create; it is a fact the person states.
DECLARE `Conduct under section 26` HAS
    `legally liable, as a master or mistress, to provide an apprentice or servant with necessary food, clothing or lodging` IS A BOOLEAN
    `wilfully refused or neglected to provide it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `had a lawful excuse for refusing or neglecting` IS A BOOLEAN
    `unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN
    `maliciously` IS A BOOLEAN
    `did or caused to be done bodily harm to the apprentice or servant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the life of the apprentice or servant was endangered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the health of the apprentice or servant has been or is likely to be permanently injured` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 26 (src:41)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 26`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26: neglecting or harming an apprentice or servant` c MEANS
        c's `legally liable, as a master or mistress, to provide an apprentice or servant with necessary food, clothing or lodging`
    AND (   (    c's `wilfully refused or neglected to provide it`
             AND NOT (c's `had a lawful excuse for refusing or neglecting`))
         OR (    c's `unlawfully`
             AND c's `maliciously`
             AND c's `did or caused to be done bodily harm to the apprentice or servant`))
    AND (   c's `the life of the apprentice or servant was endangered`
         OR c's `the health of the apprentice or servant has been or is likely to be permanently injured`)

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 26 (src:41)
GIVETH A Classification
`s 26: what the text calls the offence` MEANS misdemeanor

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 26 (src:41)
GIVETH A LIST OF Sentence
`s 26: the sentences the text states` MEANS
    LIST `penal servitude` `for a term the text does not state`

§§ `Section 27: exposing children whereby life is endangered`

-- src:42 | 27 Exposing children whereby life is endangered.
-- src:43 | Whosoever shall unlawfully abandon or expose any child, being under the age of two years, whereby the life of such child shall be endangered, or the health of such child shall have been or shall be likely to be permanently injured, shall be guilty of a misdemeanor, and being convicted thereof shall be liable . . . to be kept in penal servitude . . .
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 27 (src:42-43)
-- "being under the age of two years": younger than the second birthday, so 23 complete
-- months is under and 24 complete months is not.  "unlawfully" is in the text;
-- "maliciously" is not.
DECLARE `Conduct under section 27` HAS
    `unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN
    `abandoned or exposed a child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the age of the child in complete months` IS A NUMBER
    `the life of the child was endangered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the health of the child has been or is likely to be permanently injured` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 27 (src:43)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 27`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27: abandoning or exposing a child under two years` c MEANS
        c's `unlawfully`
    AND c's `abandoned or exposed a child`
    AND c's `the age of the child in complete months` LESS THAN 24
    AND (   c's `the life of the child was endangered`
         OR c's `the health of the child has been or is likely to be permanently injured`)

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 27 (src:43)
GIVETH A Classification
`s 27: what the text calls the offence` MEANS misdemeanor

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 27 (src:43)
GIVETH A LIST OF Sentence
`s 27: the sentences the text states` MEANS
    LIST `penal servitude` `for a term the text does not state`

§§ `Section 28: causing bodily injury by gunpowder`

-- src:44 | 28 Causing bodily injury by gunpowder.
-- src:45 | Whosoever shall unlawfully and maliciously, by the explosion of gunpowder or other explosive substance, burn, maim, disfigure, disable, or do any grievous bodily harm to any person, shall be guilty of felony, and being convicted thereof shall be liable, at the discretion of the court, to be kept in penal servitude for life . . . or to be imprisoned . . .
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 28 (src:44-45)
-- The harm must be done "by the explosion of gunpowder or other explosive substance".
-- No intent beyond "maliciously" is required.
DECLARE `Conduct under section 28` HAS
    `unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN
    `maliciously` IS A BOOLEAN
    `by the explosion of gunpowder or other explosive substance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `burnt a person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `maimed a person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `disfigured a person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `disabled a person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `did grievous bodily harm to a person` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 28 (src:45)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 28`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28: causing bodily injury by an explosion` c MEANS
        c's `unlawfully`
    AND c's `maliciously`
    AND c's `by the explosion of gunpowder or other explosive substance`
    AND (   c's `burnt a person`
         OR c's `maimed a person`
         OR c's `disfigured a person`
         OR c's `disabled a person`
         OR c's `did grievous bodily harm to a person`)

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 28 (src:45)
GIVETH A Classification
`s 28: what the text calls the offence` MEANS felony

-- "liable, at the discretion of the court, to be kept in penal servitude for life . . .
-- or to be imprisoned . . .": two options, and the term of the second is not stated.
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 28 (src:45)
GIVETH A LIST OF Sentence
`s 28: the sentences the text states` MEANS
    LIST `penal servitude` `for life`, `imprisonment` `for a term the text does not state`

§§ `Section 29: causing gunpowder to explode, or sending to any person an explosive substance, or throwing corrosive fluid on a person, with intent to do grievous bodily harm`

-- src:46 | 29 Causing gunpowder to explode, or sending to any person an explosive substance, or throwing corrosive fluid on a person, with intent to do grievous bodily harm.
-- src:47 | Whosoever shall unlawfully and maliciously cause any gunpowder or other explosive substance to explode, or send or deliver to or cause to be taken or received by any person any explosive substance or any other dangerous or noxious thing, or put or lay at any place, or cast or throw at or upon or otherwise apply to any person, any corrosive fluid or any destructive or explosive substance, with intent in any of the cases aforesaid to burn, maim, disfigure, or disable any person, or to do some grievous bodily harm to any person, shall, whether any bodily injury be effected or not, be guilty of felony, and being convicted thereof shall be liable, at the discretion of the court, to be kept in penal servitude for life . . . or to be imprisoned . . .
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 29 (src:46-47)
-- Four ways of acting (any): cause an explosion; send or deliver (or cause to be taken
-- or received) an explosive substance or other dangerous or noxious thing; put or lay
-- at any place a corrosive fluid or a destructive or explosive substance; cast, throw
-- at or upon, or otherwise apply to any person such a fluid or substance.  An intent
-- (either): to burn, maim, disfigure or disable any person, or to do some grievous
-- bodily harm to any person.  "whether any bodily injury be effected or not": injury
-- is carried in the record only so that a test can show that it makes no difference.
DECLARE `Conduct under section 29` HAS
    `unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN
    `maliciously` IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused gunpowder or another explosive substance to explode` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sent or delivered to a person, or caused to be taken or received by a person, an explosive substance or other dangerous or noxious thing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `put or laid at a place a corrosive fluid or a destructive or explosive substance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `cast or threw at or upon, or otherwise applied to, a person a corrosive fluid or a destructive or explosive substance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended to burn, maim, disfigure or disable a person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended to do some grievous bodily harm to a person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `bodily injury was effected` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 29 (src:47)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 29`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 29: causing an explosion, or sending or applying a dangerous thing, with intent` c MEANS
        c's `unlawfully`
    AND c's `maliciously`
    AND (   c's `caused gunpowder or another explosive substance to explode`
         OR c's `sent or delivered to a person, or caused to be taken or received by a person, an explosive substance or other dangerous or noxious thing`
         OR c's `put or laid at a place a corrosive fluid or a destructive or explosive substance`
         OR c's `cast or threw at or upon, or otherwise applied to, a person a corrosive fluid or a destructive or explosive substance`)
    AND (   c's `intended to burn, maim, disfigure or disable a person`
         OR c's `intended to do some grievous bodily harm to a person`)

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 29 (src:47)
GIVETH A Classification
`s 29: what the text calls the offence` MEANS felony

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 29 (src:47)
GIVETH A LIST OF Sentence
`s 29: the sentences the text states` MEANS
    LIST `penal servitude` `for life`, `imprisonment` `for a term the text does not state`

§§ `Section 30: placing gunpowder near a building, with intent to do bodily injury to any person`

-- src:48 | 30 Placing gunpowder near a building, with intent to do bodily injury to any person.
-- src:49 | Whosoever shall unlawfully and maliciously place or throw in, into, upon, against, or near any building, ship, or vessel any gunpowder or other explosive substance, with intent to do any bodily injury to any person, shall, whether or not any explosion take place, and whether or not any bodily injury be effected, be guilty of felony, and being convicted thereof shall be liable, at the discretion of the court, to be kept in penal servitude for any term not exceeding fourteen years . . . or to be imprisoned . . .
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 30 (src:48-49)
-- "whether or not any explosion take place, and whether or not any bodily injury be
-- effected": neither fact is an element; both are carried so that a test can show it.
DECLARE `Conduct under section 30` HAS
    `unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN
    `maliciously` IS A BOOLEAN
    `placed or threw in, into, upon, against or near a building, ship or vessel gunpowder or another explosive substance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended to do bodily injury to a person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an explosion took place` IS A BOOLEAN
    `bodily injury was effected` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 30 (src:49)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 30`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 30: placing an explosive near a building, ship or vessel, with intent` c MEANS
        c's `unlawfully`
    AND c's `maliciously`
    AND c's `placed or threw in, into, upon, against or near a building, ship or vessel gunpowder or another explosive substance`
    AND c's `intended to do bodily injury to a person`

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 30 (src:49)
GIVETH A Classification
`s 30: what the text calls the offence` MEANS felony

-- "penal servitude for any term not exceeding fourteen years . . . or to be imprisoned
-- . . .": 14 years = 168 months for the first option; the second option's term is not
-- stated.
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 30 (src:49)
GIVETH A LIST OF Sentence
`s 30: the sentences the text states` MEANS
    LIST `penal servitude` (`for a term not exceeding` 168), `imprisonment` `for a term the text does not state`

§§ `Section 31: setting spring guns, &c., with intent to inflict grievous bodily harm`

-- src:50 | 31 Setting spring guns, &c., with intent to inflict grievous bodily harm.
-- src:51 | Whosoever shall set or place, or cause to be set or placed, any spring gun, man trap, or other engine calculated to destroy human life or inflict grievous bodily harm, with the intent that the same or whereby the same may destroy or inflict grievous bodily harm upon a trespasser or other person coming in contact therewith, shall be guilty of a misdemeanor, and being convicted thereof shall be liable . . . to be kept in penal servitude . . . ; and whosoever shall knowingly and wilfully permit any such spring gun, man trap, or other engine which may have been set or placed in any place then being in or afterwards coming into his possession or occupation by some other person to continue so set or placed, shall be deemed to have set and placed such gun, trap, or engine with such intent as aforesaid: Provided, that nothing in this section contained shall extend to make it illegal to set or place any gin or trap such as may have been or may be usually set or placed with the intent of destroying vermin: Provided also, that nothing in this section shall be deemed to make it unlawful to set or place, or cause to be set or placed, or to be continued set or placed, from sunset to sunrise, any spring gun, man trap, or other engine which shall be set or placed, or caused or continued to be set or placed, in a dwelling house, for the protection thereof.
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 31 (src:50-51)
-- Setting: setting or placing, or causing to be set or placed, a spring gun, man trap
-- or other engine calculated to destroy human life or inflict grievous bodily harm,
-- "with the intent that the same or whereby the same may destroy or inflict grievous
-- bodily harm upon a trespasser or other person coming in contact therewith".
-- FORK (see NOTES.md): the encoding reads the phrase as two alternative intents:
-- (i) the intent that the engine destroy or inflict harm, and (ii) the intent that the
-- engine be set so that it MAY destroy or inflict harm.
-- Permitting: whoever "shall knowingly and wilfully permit any such spring gun, man
-- trap, or other engine which may have been set or placed in any place then being in
-- or afterwards coming into his possession or occupation by some other person to
-- continue so set or placed, shall be deemed to have set and placed such gun, trap, or
-- engine with such intent as aforesaid".
-- Two provisos: a gin or trap of the kind usually set to destroy vermin; and an engine
-- set, placed or continued from sunset to sunrise in a dwelling house for the
-- protection of the dwelling house.  FORK: the encoding lets the first proviso cover
-- both ways in, because the permitting limb deems the person to have set the engine.
DECLARE `Conduct under section 31` HAS
    `the engine is a spring gun, man trap or other engine calculated to destroy human life or inflict grievous bodily harm` IS A BOOLEAN
    `set or placed it, or caused it to be set or placed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended that it should destroy or inflict grievous bodily harm upon a trespasser or other person coming in contact with it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended it to be set so that it may destroy or inflict grievous bodily harm upon a trespasser or other person coming in contact with it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knowingly and wilfully permitted it, set or placed by some other person in a place then in or afterwards coming into the person's possession or occupation, to continue so set or placed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a gin or trap of the kind usually set or placed with the intent of destroying vermin` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was set, placed or continued from sunset to sunrise in a dwelling house for the protection of the dwelling house` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 31 (src:51)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 31`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 31: setting a spring gun or man trap` c MEANS
        c's `the engine is a spring gun, man trap or other engine calculated to destroy human life or inflict grievous bodily harm`
    AND (   (    c's `set or placed it, or caused it to be set or placed`
             AND (   c's `intended that it should destroy or inflict grievous bodily harm upon a trespasser or other person coming in contact with it`
                  OR c's `intended it to be set so that it may destroy or inflict grievous bodily harm upon a trespasser or other person coming in contact with it`))
         OR c's `knowingly and wilfully permitted it, set or placed by some other person in a place then in or afterwards coming into the person's possession or occupation, to continue so set or placed`)
    AND NOT (c's `it is a gin or trap of the kind usually set or placed with the intent of destroying vermin`)
    AND NOT (c's `it was set, placed or continued from sunset to sunrise in a dwelling house for the protection of the dwelling house`)

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 31 (src:51)
GIVETH A Classification
`s 31: what the text calls the offence` MEANS misdemeanor

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 31 (src:51)
GIVETH A LIST OF Sentence
`s 31: the sentences the text states` MEANS
    LIST `penal servitude` `for a term the text does not state`
